            <note corresp="#d40-f2" n="2" xml:id="d40-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d39">Document 39</ref> and <ref target="#d39-f2">footnote 2
                        thereto</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f3" n="3" xml:id="d40-f3-content">
                <p>In a September 19 memorandum to Packard,
                        Johnson, and Helms, Kissinger requested that they expand the NSSM 99 response to include an option that would
                    allow Cambodian forces to defend the area outlined in variant 3 of Strategy 3
                    without “significant long term intervention by South Vietnamese.” (National
                    Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials,
                        NSC Files, NSC Institutional Files (H-Files), Box H–173, NSSM Files, NSSM
                    99)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
